  "img": "systems/pf1/icons/skills/illusion_01.jpg",
  "name": "Illusionist",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>The illusionist class is a master of perception, weaving intricate tapestries of light, sound, and false reality to outwit and confound their adversaries. Unlike traditional elemental mages or direct damage dealers, their power lies in manipulating the very senses of their foes, turning the battlefield into a stage for their elaborate deceits. An illusionist might conjure spectral duplicates to absorb attacks, manifest terrifying figments that send enemies fleeing in terror, or create phantom landscapes to disorient and control the flow of combat, all while rarely needing to land a direct blow.</em></p><h2>Role</h2><p>The illusionist thrives not on direct damage or healing, but on the power of deception and perception manipulation, making them the ultimate tricksters and tactical controllers of the battlefield. Their primary role is to sow confusion among enemies, creating deceptive doubles to draw aggro, conjuring phantom obstacles to control movement, or weaving shrouds of mist to conceal allies and critical objectives. Beyond combat, they are invaluable for infiltration, espionage, and social manipulation, able to craft convincing disguises, generate perfect distractions, or make a seemingly impassable barrier appear (or disappear) with a flick of their wrist. They excel at turning a party's weaknesses into strengths by making them elusive, turning a difficult encounter into an easily bypassed charade, and ultimately dictating the flow of any situation through cunning and misdirection rather than brute force.</p><h2>Class Skills</h2><p>The illusionist's class skills are Bluff (Cha), Craft (Int), Diplomacy (Cha), Disguise (Cha), Knowledge (arcana) (Int), Knowledge (local) (Int), Knowledge (planes) (Int), Linguistics (Int), Perception (Wis), Perform (Cha), Profession (Wis), Sense Motive (Wis), Sleight of Hands (Dex), Spellcraft (Int), and Stealth (Dex).</p><h2>Weapon and Armor Proficiency</h2><p>Illusionists are proficient with the dagger, sling, power rod, power staff, and quarterstaff, but not with any type of armor or shield. Heavier armor interferes with an illusionist's movements, which can cause his spells with somatic components to fail.</p><h2>Main Ability Score</h2><p>The illusionist mainly focuses on DEX for combat, and CHA for his class features and spells.</p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
